PROGRAM 9 — Java & Jenkins Installation
Q: Install Java and Jenkins (prerequisite setup for CI/CD).
----------------------------------------------------------------
Step 1: Install Java SE (JDK 17/21) for Windows
  - Download Java SE Archive (Windows x64 installer)
  - Run the .exe -> Install

Step 2: Verify installation
  C:\ -> Program Files -> Java -> jdk-21/17 -> bin -> copy path

Step 3: Set environment variable
  Windows + S -> "Environment Variables" -> Environment Variables
  System variables -> New
    Variable name: JavaDevOps (any name)
    Variable value: <paste JDK bin path>
  -> OK
  System variables -> Path -> Edit -> New
    %JavaDevOps%\bin -> OK

Step 4: Verify in Command Prompt
  java --version

Step 5: Create a Jenkins test job
  - Create file hello.py with: print("hello jenkins")
  - Commit/save the file
  - Configure Jenkins job to run it (see Program 10)
  Expected output: "hello jenkins" -> Finished: SUCCESS

