PROGRAM 10 — Create a Project Using Jenkins
Q: Create a Jenkins project that pulls from GitHub and runs a 
build step.
----------------------------------------------------------------
Step 1: GitHub setup
  - Log in to GitHub -> Create new repository (e.g., "Project10")
  - Add README -> Create repository
  - Add file -> Create new file
    type: print("hello jenkins")
    Save as: hello.py (Python file)
  - Commit changes

Step 2: Jenkins plugin & tool setup
  - Manage Jenkins -> Plugins -> Installed Plugins (verify Git plugin)
  - Manage Jenkins -> Tools -> search "Git installation"
    Path: <copy path of git.exe install location> -> Save

Step 3: Add credentials
  - Manage Jenkins -> Credentials -> System -> Global credentials
    -> Add Credentials
    Username: <your name>
    Password: <GitHub token>
  -> Create

Step 4: Create the Jenkins Job
  - New Item -> Enter item name (e.g., "Project9")
  - Select "Freestyle project" -> OK
  - Scroll to "Source Code Management" -> select Git
    Repository URL: <paste GitHub repo URL>
    Credentials: select the one created above
    Branch Specifier: change "master" -> "main"
  - (Optional) Additional Behaviours -> Add -> "Check out to a
    sub-directory"

Step 5: Add Build Step
  - Build Steps -> Add build step -> "Execute Windows batch command"
    Command: python hello.py
  - Apply and Save

Step 6: Build
  - Click "Build Now"
  - Console Output should show: hello jenkins
    Finished: SUCCESS

